<section class="section" aria-labelledby="job-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="job-title">Job work between units</h2>
      <p>Garment work often moves between several units for cutting, stitching, embroidery and washing. Section 143 of the CGST Act lets a registered principal send inputs out without paying tax, and on to further job workers. The principal keeps responsibility for proper accounts.</p>
      <p class="para">Inputs have one year, and capital goods three years, to come back or be supplied from there. Moulds, dies, jigs, fixtures and tools are outside those limits. A goods-out register by job worker is the simple control. See {% routeLink "/industries/accounting-for-manufacturers/", "accounting for manufacturers" %}.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Staff and buildings</h2>
      <p>A factory with many workers usually has payroll and employee insurance and provident fund duties. See {% routeLink "/services/payroll-services/", "payroll" %}. If you rent out or sublet part of your premises, as this area becomes more mixed, ask how that income should be shown, and whether your lease allows it.</p>
      <p class="para">AccountOrbit has no office in Okhla, and takes enquiries by phone from anywhere in Delhi. If you export, your list of export invoices with shipping and payment dates is the first thing worth sharing.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

